{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-200720-r4516598","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Grilled Pork Tenderloin","sourcePageId":200720,"sourceRevision":"4516598","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-20T19:10:45Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Grilled%20Pork%20Tenderloin&oldid=4516598","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:54:35.000Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Grilled recipes","Category:Main course recipes","Category:Marinade recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for spice mixes","Category:Recipes using apple cider","Category:Recipes using cayenne","Category:Recipes using chipotle chile","Category:Recipes using honey","Category:Recipes using lime juice","Category:Recipes using pork","Category:Recipes using vegetable oil","Category:Recipes using vinegar","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"cf24229e9a20c0726f63e3c648bb9feaf145139a95514719c425930d983a3ab0","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__\n{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Pork recipes\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\n== Ingredients ==\n\n=== '''Marinade''' ===\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Each|ea]]. (~2.25 [[Cookbook:Pound|lb]] / 1 [[Cookbook:Kilogram|kg]]) [[Cookbook:Pork|pork]] tenderloin, trimmed\n* ¼ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] freshly-squeezed [[Cookbook:Lime|lime]] juice\n* ¼ cup [[Cookbook:Honey|honey]]\n* 1 ½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] apple [[Cookbook:Cider Vinegar|cider vinegar]]\n* ¼ cup [[Cookbook:Apple Cider|apple cider]]\n\n=== '''Rub''' ===\n* 2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Paprika|paprika]]\n* ½ tbsp [[Cookbook:Garlic Powder|garlic powder]]\n* 1 ⅓ tbsp [[Cookbook:Cayenne Pepper|cayenne pepper]]\n* ½ tbsp [[Cookbook:Chipotle Pepper|chipotle]] powder\n* ½ tbsp [[Cookbook:Black Pepper|black pepper]]\n* ½ tbsp dried [[Cookbook:Rosemary|rosemary]]\n\n=== '''Grill''' ===\n* 4 lb natural chunk charcoal\n* ½ pound soaked applewood chips\n* 2 tsp [[Cookbook:Vegetable oil|vegetable oil]]\n* 1 sheet newspaper\n\n== Procedure ==\n#Combine marinade ingredients in a small [[Cookbook:Saucepan|saucepan]]. Pour half into a large zip-top plastic bag, reserving the other half in the fridge. Add pork to the bag, remove extra air, and [[Cookbook:Marinating|marinate]] in the fridge for 24 hours.\n#Remove pork from marinade. Discard the bag and the marinade in the bag. Allow the pork to drain as necessary.\n#Combine rub ingredients, and rub all over pork.\n#Moisten newspaper with oil and wad up under a large chimney starter with charcoal in it. Light and wait 15 minutes.\n#Once charcoal has heated, disperse evenly around bottom of grill. Add soaked chips, replace grate, and place pork in the center. Cover and cook for 1 ½ minutes (or a bit more, use your judgment).\n#Flip to another side and cook 1 ½ more minutes and repeat until pork has cooked for at least 12 minutes and until the internal temperature reaches at least 145°F (63˚C).\n#Make a large [[Cookbook:Aluminium Foil|foil]] pouch (or use a covered dish) and place pork inside. Pour in reserved marinade (warmed to at least 145°F) and let rest for 10 minutes.\n#Serve.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using pork]]\n[[Category:Recipes using honey]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lime juice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using vinegar]]\n[[Category:Marinade recipes]]\n[[Category:Grilled recipes]]\n[[Category:Main course recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for spice mixes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using apple cider]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chipotle chile]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cayenne]]\n[[Category:Recipes using vegetable oil]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Grilled Pork Tenderloin","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 ea. (~2.25 lb / 1 kg) pork tenderloin, trimmed","sourceText":"1 ea. (~2.25 lb / 1 kg) pork tenderloin, trimmed","amountText":"1 ea. (~2.25 lb / 1 kg) pork tenderloin, trimmed","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"¼ cup freshly-squeezed lime juice","sourceText":"¼ cup freshly-squeezed lime juice","amountText":"¼ cup freshly-squeezed lime juice","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"¼ cup honey","sourceText":"¼ cup honey","amountText":"¼ cup honey","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 ½ tsp salt","sourceText":"1 ½ tsp salt","amountText":"1 ½ tsp salt","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"2 tbsp apple cider vinegar","sourceText":"2 tbsp apple cider vinegar","amountText":"2 tbsp apple cider vinegar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"¼ cup apple cider","sourceText":"¼ cup apple cider","amountText":"¼ cup apple cider","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"2 tbsp paprika","sourceText":"2 tbsp paprika","amountText":"2 tbsp paprika","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"½ tbsp garlic powder","sourceText":"½ tbsp garlic powder","amountText":"½ tbsp garlic powder","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-9","name":"1 ⅓ tbsp cayenne pepp